Figure 4: Comparison of the constraints on the structure growth parameter, $S_{8}$. Dots represent the posterior median, the $16$-th and the $84$-th percentiles are delimited by the bars. From top to bottom: 3D
cluster clustering in the AMICO KiDS-1000 catalogue obtained in this work (green), with the green-shaded band that reproduces its uncertainty for a visual comparison; AMICO KiDS-1000 joint weak lensing and number counts from Lesci et al. (2025, gold); AMICO KiDS-DR3 3D cluster clustering from Lesci et al. (2022b, pale blue); AMICO KiDS-DR3 angular cluster clustering from Romanello et al. (2024, dark orange);
eROSITA All-Sky Survey number counts from Ghirardini et al. (2024, navy blue);
DES cluster counts from Abbott et al. (2025, red); HSC plus SDSS joint modelling of weak lensing, number counts and clustering from Sunayama et al. (2024, purple); SPT cluster counts from Bocquet et al. (2024, teal); and eROSITA eFEDS from Chiu et al. (2023, yellow). Finally, we list measurements not based on cluster cosmology, such as KiDS-Legacy and KiDS-1000 Cosmic Shear constraints from Wright et al. (2025, brown) and Asgari et al. (2021, royalblue); CMB results from (Planck+18, black) and WMAP (Hinshaw et al. 2013, magenta).

Figure 1: Marginalised posterior of the Linear-kernel amplitude $A$ for CC,
DESI DR1 and DESI DR2. All three are consistent with the $\Lambda\mathrm{CDM}$ value $A=0$;
DR2 gives the tightest bound, $A=-0.000\pm 0.031$.
